Netflix is revolutionising the way we watch TV, but some fear that Netflix could be closing the curtains on the big screen.

429
01:20:11,059 --> 01:20:16,960
So, is there any evidence to suggest that our love for streaming movies at home could sell the end to cinema?

430
01:20:17,679 --> 01:20:22,159
US-based company Netflix has had more than a few reasons to celebrate this.

431
01:20:22,699 --> 01:20:31,960
It's added a record-breaking number of paid users to its online streaming service in 2018, now topping 139 million worldwide.

432
01:20:31,960 --> 01:20:35,359
That's three times the number of accounts just five years ago.

433
01:20:35,599 --> 01:20:40,920
Keep in mind that more than one person could be using an account, so its reach is even bigger.

434
01:20:41,739 --> 01:20:47,819
The USA is Netflix's top market globally, with over 40% of all paid users based there.

435
01:20:48,099 --> 01:20:54,420
The company has also invested heavily into producing original content, including big movie blockbusters.

436
01:20:54,759 --> 01:21:01,579
Analysts estimate that the company spent $13 billion on titles like Narcos and Bird Box in 2018.

437
01:21:01,960 --> 01:21:08,199
That would be enough to make Titanic one of the most expensive films ever made 65 times.

438
01:21:08,639 --> 01:21:10,399
Its efforts seem to be paying off.

439
01:21:10,920 --> 01:21:19,259
This year, its critically acclaimed film Roma has earned a streaming service, its first Best Picture Oscar nomination, with 10 in total.

440
01:21:19,259 --> 01:21:33,039
You might think that can only benefit the box office, but Netflix has been criticised for showing films in a relatively small number of movie theaters, and for a limited time, before streaming them on its own site.

441
01:21:33,779 --> 01:21:36,779
So, are there any signs that cinemas are suffering?

442
01:21:36,779 --> 01:21:38,359
Not really.

443
01:21:39,000 --> 01:21:45,420
While analysts said that 2017 was a tough year for movie movies, last year saw a boost for the box office.

444
01:21:46,059 --> 01:21:49,799
Worldwide, cinemas made over $41.5 billion.

445
01:21:50,500 --> 01:21:53,460
That's 2.6% more than in 2017.

446
01:21:54,019 --> 01:21:59,960
The top three markets, the USA, China and the UK, all saw increases in revenue to change.

447
01:21:59,960 --> 01:22:04,779
And moviegoers in America generated nearly $12 billion for the industry.

448
01:22:05,579 --> 01:22:13,859
There are other reasons to be sceptical of the suggestions that the rising popularity of Netflix is to blame for the perceived decline of cinema.

449
01:22:14,699 --> 01:22:21,299
Comparing the trends in cinema revenues and streaming services tells us little about how one impacts the other.

450
01:22:21,299 --> 01:22:31,359
Just like the consumption of mozzarella cheese can't really explain the rise in the number of civil engineering doctorates awarded, even though they're both going up.

451
01:22:31,659 --> 01:22:40,759
There are a number of other factors at play, which are likely to contribute to the possible success or failure of cinemas and streaming services.

452
01:22:41,979 --> 01:22:48,500
But, is there any evidence to suggest that Netflix and movie theaters are competing for audiences?

453
01:22:48,500 --> 01:22:50,839
That's a tricky one too.

454
01:22:51,420 --> 01:22:59,239
One US study by NATO, that's the National Association of Theater Owners in the States, not the North Atlantic Treaty Organization.

455
01:23:00,019 --> 01:23:08,139
So there's just under 2,000 people in the US who both streamed content and saw at least one film in the cinema over the last year.

456
01:23:08,619 --> 01:23:17,979
They found that people who watch a lot of stream programs also go to the cinema frequently, while those who don't subscribe rarely visit the movie theaters either.

457
01:23:18,500 --> 01:23:25,539
But even that doesn't tell us conclusively about how the use of one platform actually affects people's cinema habits.

458
01:23:26,179 --> 01:23:32,379
